msgid "inventory.overview.about_title"
msgstr "How stock is kept"

msgid "inventory.overview.about"
msgstr "On-hand quantity is a projection of an immutable double-entry ledger. Receipts, deliveries, transfers, adjustments, and RMAs post debit and credit lines. Valuation follows each product’s costing method (FIFO, LIFO, moving average, or standard). Completing an operation posts the journal; you cannot edit ledger rows by hand."

msgid "inventory.products.title"
msgstr "Products"

msgid "inventory.products.subtitle"
msgstr "Templates with tracking, costing, and dispatch strategy. Variants are the SKUs you stock."

msgid "inventory.variants.title"
msgstr "SKUs / variants"

msgid "inventory.variants.subtitle"
msgstr "Buy, stock, and sell units, barcodes (UPC/EAN), and standard cost."

msgid "inventory.uom_groups.title"
msgstr "Unit groups"

msgid "inventory.uom_groups.subtitle"
msgstr "Conversions only apply inside the same group (count, weight, volume)."

msgid "inventory.uoms.title"
msgstr "Units of measure"

msgid "inventory.uoms.subtitle"
msgstr "Ratio is how many reference units one of this UoM contains (dozen = 12)."

msgid "inventory.attributes.title"
msgstr "Attributes"

msgid "inventory.attributes.subtitle"
msgstr "Dynamic catalog attributes (color, size, grade) for product variants."

msgid "inventory.attribute_values.title"
msgstr "Attribute values"

msgid "inventory.attribute_values.subtitle"
msgstr "Allowed values for select-type attributes."

msgid "inventory.locations.title"
msgstr "Locations"

msgid "inventory.locations.subtitle"
msgstr "Warehouses down to bins, plus virtual locations for suppliers, customers, transit, scrap, and adjustments."

msgid "inventory.locations.tree"
msgstr "Hierarchy"

msgid "inventory.locations.add"
msgstr "Add location"

msgid "inventory.locations.detail"
msgstr "Location"

msgid "inventory.locations.count"
msgstr "%d locations"

msgid "inventory.stock.title"
msgstr "Stock on hand"

msgid "inventory.stock.subtitle"
msgstr "Balances by SKU, location, and lot. Quantity is ledger-controlled."

msgid "inventory.lots.title"
msgstr "Lots / batches"

msgid "inventory.lots.subtitle"
msgstr "Expiry and manufactured dates drive FEFO dispatch and recalls."

msgid "inventory.serials.title"
msgstr "Serial numbers"

msgid "inventory.serials.subtitle"
msgstr "End-to-end identity for serialized items."

msgid "inventory.operations.title"
msgstr "Warehouse operations"

msgid "inventory.operations.subtitle"
msgstr "Create an operation, add stock moves, then set state to Done to post the ledger."

msgid "inventory.operations.header"
msgstr "Operation"

msgid "inventory.operations.hint"
msgstr "Draft → Assigned (reserves quantity) → Done (posts debit/credit). Cancelled operations cannot be completed."

msgid "inventory.moves.title"
msgstr "Stock moves"

msgid "inventory.moves.hint"
msgstr "Each line credits the source location and debits the destination. Lot-tracked products require a lot; serial-tracked products require a serial."

msgid "inventory.receipts.title"
msgstr "Receipts"

msgid "inventory.receipts.subtitle"
msgstr "Inbound receiving: match a PO origin, optional QC status, then complete to put away."

msgid "inventory.fulfillment.title"
msgstr "Fulfillment"

msgid "inventory.fulfillment.subtitle"
msgstr "Outbound picks. Use wave and batch on the operation for wave/zone/batch picking."

msgid "inventory.transfers.title"
msgstr "Internal transfers"

msgid "inventory.transfers.subtitle"
msgstr "Move stock between locations or warehouses. Transit locations track stock in flight."

msgid "inventory.adjustments.title"
msgstr "Adjustments & cycle counts"

msgid "inventory.adjustments.subtitle"
msgstr "Set counted quantity and mark Done. The difference posts against the inventory-adjustment location."

msgid "inventory.returns.title"
msgstr "Returns / RMA"

msgid "inventory.returns.subtitle"
msgstr "Set state to Received to bring stock back. Disposition chooses restock, repair, quarantine, scrap, or credit-only."

msgid "inventory.planning.title"
msgstr "Reorder rules"

msgid "inventory.planning.subtitle"
msgstr "Safety stock: reorder point = demand × lead time + safety stock. Min/max uses min as the reorder point. Forecast uses the same lead-time model until a demand history feed is connected."

msgid "inventory.ledger.title"
msgstr "Stock ledger"

msgid "inventory.ledger.subtitle"
msgstr "Immutable debit and credit lines. This is the audit trail for quantity and value."

msgid "inventory.cost_layers.title"
msgstr "Cost layers"

msgid "inventory.cost_layers.subtitle"
msgstr "Remaining FIFO/LIFO/average layers created on inbound and consumed on outbound."

msgid "inventory.hardware.title"
msgstr "Warehouse devices"

msgid "inventory.hardware.subtitle"
msgstr "Registry for barcode scanners, RFID readers, mobile apps, and MQTT/Bluetooth sensors. Pairing and telemetry are extension points."

msgid "inventory.integrations.title"
msgstr "Integrations"

msgid "inventory.integrations.subtitle"
msgstr "Webhook and ERP connector records (SAP, NetSuite, Odoo, commerce, CRM). Delivery is event-driven from the stock ledger."

